  "PhotoPath": "",
  "Caption": "The order was saved, but the confirmation email never went out.\n\nThe database and the message broker don\u0027t share a transaction. If the process crashes between SaveChanges and Publish, the two systems drift apart and nobody gets an error.\n\nThe fix is the Transactional Outbox:\n1. Save the message in an OutboxMessages table, in the same transaction as the order\n2. A background worker reads it and publishes it\n3. Mark it as sent\n\nThe guarantee is at-least-once delivery, so consumers must be idempotent (the Inbox pattern).\n\nTools: MassTransit Outbox, CAP, Wolverine.\n\n#Microservices #EventDriven #DotNet #Architecture",
